ext":"ClientAuthMethod","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientauthmethod","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How a client proves its identity at the token endpoint (RFC 8705 §2, OIDC Core §9 naming)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Only the methods AXIAM actually implements are representable. There is deliberately no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"none"},{"type":"text","text":" variant: every AXIAM client is confidential today (see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"handle_authorization_code"},{"type":"text","text":"),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and adding a public-client value here before the rest of the server understands one would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"let an operator register a client whose authentication is silently skipped."}]}}}